263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 186 0 R
/E (A cloud environment is a dynamic platform that provides the required resources, storage, services and many more over the internet. The rapid increase in usage of cloud environments for it's efficiency, scalability and fast computation, can also come with the performance degradation and failures. Here health assessment plays a crucial role by predicting the failures in advance. The existing systems are using single machine learning models and are able to detect but after the failures has already occurred and they lack the full architecture of classifying systems in different states. They are heavily depended on the historical data storage. To address these all limitations this project proposes a stateless cloud monitoring system that will combine the performance prediction and health assessment using ensemble machine learning models. It enables the early detection of all possible failures. Multiple machine learning models will be used together to predict the performance behavior and classify the system as Normal, Warning, or Critical accordingly. The system is going to depend on real time rather than the )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
