431 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (The development of cloud monitoring and predictive health assessment systems has gained significant attention in recent years due to the increasing complexity and scale of cloud computing environments. Traditional monitoring systems primarily rely on single machine learning models to observe system behavior and detect anomalies. While these approaches provide basic insights, they often face several limitations, including a reactive nature where issues are identified only after they occur, a heavy dependency on large volumes of historical data, and a lack of ability to classify system states into clear, actionable categories for decision-making. As cloud infrastructures continue to grow in size and dynamic behavior, these limitations reduce the effectiveness of conventional monitoring solutions. In response to these challenges, recent research has focused on enhancing prediction accuracy and system intelligence through advanced machine learning techniques, particularly ensemble learning methods. Ensemble approaches combine multiple models to improve robustness, reduce bias and variance, and provide more reliable predictions compared to single-model systems. This literature review explores recent advancements in the application of ensemble machine learning for cloud performance prediction and health assessment, highlighting how these techniques enable proactive monitoring, better anomaly detection, and more meaningful classification of system health. By integrating predictive capabilities with classification mechanisms, modern systems are moving toward more efficient, scalable, and future-aware cloud management solutions.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
432 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (The scope of this project is to develop a machine learning-based system that can monitor and predict cloud performance in real time without relying heavily on historical data. The system focuses on building a simple and scalable stateless model that provides early insights into system health, helping in proactive issue detection. It aims to improve performance monitoring, reduce downtime, and enhance resource utilization. Additionally, the project can be extended to detect anomalies, predict failures, and support efficient decision-making in cloud environments. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
