/T (The project begins with the requirements and setup phase, where data schemas are defined, hardware and software environments are configured, appropriate datasets are selected, and the foundation of the Flask backend is established. Following this, the core machine learning development phase focuses on implementing the performance prediction module along with the system health classification module. Once the ML components are ready, the next step involves API and frontend integration, where the machine learning pipeline is exposed through Flask RESTful APIs and connected to a React or HTML-based frontend dashboard for user interaction and visualization. Finally, in the testing and deployment phase, the system is thoroughly evaluated by testing machine learning model outputs and API endpoints, using metrics such as MAE and RMSE for regression tasks, and Accuracy along with the Confusion Matrix for classification tasks to ensure reliability and performance.)
/E (The project begins with the requirements and setup phase, where data schemas are defined, hardware and software environments are configured, appropriate datasets are selected, and the foundation of the Flask backend is established. Following this, the core machine learning development phase focuses on implementing the performance prediction module along with the system health classification module. Once the ML components are ready, the next step involves API and frontend integration, where the machine learning pipeline is exposed through Flask RESTful APIs and connected to a React or HTML-based frontend dashboard for user interaction and visualization. Finally, in the testing and deployment phase, the system is thoroughly evaluated by testing machine learning model outputs and API endpoints, using metrics such as MAE and RMSE for regression tasks, and Accuracy along with the Confusion Matrix for classification tasks to ensure reliability and performance.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [19]
>>
