/T (In the data preparation stage, the collected cloud data is thoroughly cleaned and preprocessed to remove noise, missing values, and inconsistencies that could negatively impact model performance. This step also involves normalizing and transforming the data into a well-structured format that is suitable for machine learning algorithms, ensuring that all features are properly aligned for analysis. Once the data is prepared, the analysis stage begins, where multiple machine learning models such as Decision Tree, Random Forest, and Logistic Regression are applied to examine the dataset. )
/E (In the data preparation stage, the collected cloud data is thoroughly cleaned and preprocessed to remove noise, missing values, and inconsistencies that could negatively impact model performance. This step also involves normalizing and transforming the data into a well-structured format that is suitable for machine learning algorithms, ensuring that all features are properly aligned for analysis. Once the data is prepared, the analysis stage begins, where multiple machine learning models such as Decision Tree, Random Forest, and Logistic Regression are applied to examine the dataset. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
