/E (The system can be developed and deployed on operating systems such as Windows 10/11, macOS, or Linux, providing flexibility across different environments. It requires Python 3.9 or higher as the primary programming language runtime. For backend development, Flask 2.x is used to build and manage RESTful APIs. The machine learning components rely on libraries such as scikit-learn for model building, along with pandas and numpy for data manipulation and numerical computations. On the frontend, technologies like HTML, CSS, and JavaScript or frameworks such as React can be used to create an interactive user interface. Additionally, development and testing tools like Visual Studio Code for coding, Postman for API testing, and Git for version control are utilized to streamline the development process.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
