<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (The system is composed of several key components that work together to ensure efficient data processing, accurate prediction, and clear result presentation. The System Metrics component manages input data such as CPU usage, memory usage, disk I/O, network traffic, and timestamp, and includes methods like collect_data\(\) and preprocess\(\) to gather, clean, and prepare the data for further analysis. The Regression Model component focuses on predicting future system performance using algorithms like Random Forest and Gradient Boosting, with methods such as train\(\), predict\(\), and ensemble_average\(\) to enhance accuracy through ensemble learning techniques. The Classification Model component includes Decision Tree, Random Forest, and Logistic Regression classifiers, and uses methods like train\(\), predict\(\), and voting_classifier\(\) to analyze the data and determine the overall system health more reliably. The Health Status component stores and interprets the final classification results, including system status \(Normal, Warning, or Critical\) and risk level \(Low, Medium, or High\), using the evaluate\(\) method to make the output meaningful and easy to understand. Finally, the Report component is responsible for generating structured summaries of predictions and classifications, with features like generate_report\(\) and export_pdf\(\) that allow users to view, download, and share the results conveniently, improving usability and decision-making.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
