/E (The cloud health prediction system uses multiple machine learning techniques to improve accuracy and reliability. First, a Decision Tree classifies the system state as Normal, Warning, or Critical based on predefined thresholds, such as CPU usage above 85% being Critical, between 70% and 85% being Warning, and below 70% being Normal. Then, a Random Forest model processes the same cloud data and generates multiple independent predictions to enhance accuracy. Logistic Regression is also used to estimate the probability of the system being in each state, providing a confidence level for the prediction. Furthermore, Random Forest and Gradient Boosting models analyze the processed data to predict CPU and memory values by capturing complex patterns. These predictions are combined using Ensemble Regression, where the final output is calculated as the average of Random Forest and Gradient Boosting predictions, reducing variance and improving accuracy. Finally, a Voting Classifier combines the outputs of Decision Tree, Random Forest, and Logistic Regression, where each model votes for a system state, and the class receiving at least two out of three votes is selected as the final output, ensuring a more robust and reliable decision.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
