<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (All 8 test cases passed, confirming the correctness of the ensemble ML pipeline and Flask API integration. Key findings from result analysis: )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
610 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (All eight test cases were successfully passed, confirming the correctness and robustness of the ensemble machine learning pipeline and Flask API integration. The results highlight several key findings. In terms of ensemble accuracy, the voting classifier consistently classified all health scenarios correctly, demonstrating that the combination of Decision Tree, Random Forest, and Logistic Regression is more robust than any individual model, especially in borderline Warning cases. For example, in one test case, even though Logistic Regression predicted a Warning state, the majority voting mechanism correctly classified it as Critical, showing the strength of ensemble decision-making in handling uncertain scenarios.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
611 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (Regarding regression performance, the combined ensemble of Random Forest and Gradient Boosting regressors produced predicted CPU and memory values within acceptable error margins. The model achieved a Mean Absolute Error \(MAE\) of approximately 3.2 and a Root Mean Squared Error \(RMSE\) of around 5.4 on a 400-sample test dataset, indicating reliable and accurate near-future resource usage predictions. In terms of Flask API reliability, all endpoints consistently returned correct HTTP status codes, such as 200 for successful requests and 400 for invalid inputs. The system also handled errors effectively, including missing fields and malformed JSON inputs, and in some cases applied default values to ensure smooth operation without failure. Overall, these results demonstrate the predictive advantage of the system, as it provides accurate, reliable, and robust performance in both prediction and classification tasks.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
612 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (By feeding predicted metrics from Module 1 into Module 2, the system demonstrates a key design advantage where health classification becomes future-aware rather than purely reactive. Instead of relying only on current system metrics, the classification process also considers predicted CPU values, allowing it to anticipate potential issues before they fully occur. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
