/T (7.2 System Limitations )
/E (7.2 System Limitations )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
626 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (The current system has a few limitations that should be considered for real-world deployment. One major limitation is its dependency on synthetic or simulated datasets for training, which may not fully represent the complexity and variability of real-world cloud environments. Additionally, the system relies on static thresholds for label creation, such as defining values above 85% CPU or memory usage as Critical, which may not be suitable for all cloud infrastructures and could require customization based on specific use cases. Another concern is the lack of authentication and authorization in the Flask API, making it insecure for direct production use without implementing proper security mechanisms. Furthermore, the system is designed as a single-node application, meaning it runs on a single server, and extending it to a distributed environment across multiple cloud nodes would require additional configuration and orchestration.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
