637 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 217 0 R
/E (A Flask-based backend API manages communication between all components by exposing RESTful endpoints for prediction, health status, simulation, and retrieval of evaluation metrics, ensuring smooth data flow across the system. The frontend dashboard provides a clean and responsive user interface, featuring real-time metric visualization, interactive input controls, and chart-based trend monitoring to help users easily interpret results. During integration and system testing, all eight test cases were successfully passed, confirming the correctness of the ensemble machine learning pipeline, the reliability of the Flask API, and the seamless end-to-end data flow between frontend and backend. The system achieved a classification accuracy of approximately 83.5% and a regression MAE of around 3.21 on a held-out test dataset, demonstrating strong and reliable performance within the academic project scope.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
638 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 217 0 R
/T (8.2 Project Outcomes )
/E (8.2 Project Outcomes )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
639 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 217 0 R
/E (The project delivers a fully functional end-to-end cloud health monitoring system capable of processing raw cloud metrics such as CPU, memory, disk I/O, and network usage to generate actionable predictions and health classifications. It incorporates a dual-ensemble machine learning architecture, where ensemble averaging is used in the regression module for performance prediction and majority voting is applied in the classification module for determining system health, showcasing an advanced use of ensemble techniques at multiple stages. The system is designed to be future-aware by incorporating predicted performance values into the classification process, enabling proactive detection of potential issues before they lead to failures. Its stateless and scalable design eliminates the need for historical data storage, making it lightweight, portable, and easy to deploy across various cloud environments. The backend is implemented as a production-ready Flask RESTful API with multiple endpoints, CORS support, and proper error handling, allowing seamless integration with different frontends or monitoring tools. On the frontend, a responsive and interactive dashboard provides real-time metric visualization, prediction results, classifier vote transparency, trend charts, and resource distribution graphs for better user understanding. Additionally, the project includes a complete development setup using VS Code, featuring F5 launch support, Live Server integration, REST client testing, and well-documented configuration steps to ensure ease of development and deployment.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
