/Title (The project begins with the requirements and setup phase, where data schemas are defined, hardware and software environments are configured, appropriate datasets are selected, and the foundation of the Flask backend is established. Following this, the core machine learning development phase focuses on implementing the performance prediction module along with the system health classification module. Once the ML components are ready, the next step involves API and frontend integration, where the machine learning pipeline is exposed through Flask RESTful APIs and connected to a React or HTML-based frontend dashboard for user interaction and visualization. Finally, in the testing and deployment phase, the system is thoroughly evaluated by testing machine learning model outputs and API endpoints, using metrics such as MAE and RMSE for regression tasks, and Accuracy along with the Confusion Matrix for classification tasks to ensure reliability and performance.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1508 0 R
/Next 1503 0 R
>>
endobj
1506 0 obj
<<
/Title (In the data preparation stage, the collected cloud data is thoroughly cleaned and preprocessed to remove noise, missing values, and inconsistencies that could negatively impact model performance. This step also involves normalizing and transforming the data into a well-structured format that is suitable for machine learning algorithms, ensuring that all features are properly aligned for analysis. Once the data is prepared, the analysis stage begins, where multiple machine learning models such as Decision Tree, Random Forest, and Logistic Regression are applied to examine the dataset.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1503 0 R
>>
endobj
